"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"I WOULD HIGHLY RECOMMEND LEAVING START APPS AFTER SETUP ON!\n\nOnce everything is set up, in 'MSYS2 Setup', click 'next' then, download it in the default download path. Once MSYS finished downloading, go back to the tool and click 'DL DEPENDENCIES' on the "Setup" tab.\n\nOn the SM64 AP Launcher, click 'Compile default SM64AP build' (or 'Show advanced options' then 'Compile custom build' if you prefer).\nDoing that, a new 'Build Configurator' window should open and in there, press 'Browse...' and select the directory where your build will be located. In the input field below, enter the name of the build (call it whatever you want). Finally, you can click 'Download Files'.\nWhen it's done, you can select the region, make flags and apply patches. Once you're done, you can 'Create Build'.\n\nWhen the build is created, go back to the Launcher's 'Main Window' and you'll see the new build in 'Playable builds'. Select it and before starting, in 'Launch Options'.\n\nReplace 'NAME' by the name assigned to your YAML file.\n\nReplace 'PORT' with the port, it is a 5-digit number that can be found the Archipelago website after opening a new room.\n\nThe 'Password' field is optional. If the host did not set one, leave it to default value.\n\nFinally, you can click 'Play selected build' and start playing!",
